35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"The readmission data shows a clear drop during the trial, but it drifted back after.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Toshio,,The booking system only logs named slots. Unplanned work is invisible in reports.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,The board minutes confirm the joint clinic closed because neither department held the budget.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"Agency cover is rising, and therapy staff are leaving for city posts. Midwifery has slack.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Servas,,The development budget is down by a quarter. Off-site visits earn no tariff from the fund.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Servas, if off-site visits earn nothing, how do we justify a home follow-up team?","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Benjamin, that explains the joint clinic failure. Shared responsibility without shared cost is fatal.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Toshio, exactly. The booking system gap means we cannot even measure the workload properly.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Asuka, the midwifery slack is interesting. Maybe we can leverage that for perinatal support.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Asuka, it is a difficult question. We must find a model that generates on-site revenue.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,The shared nursing round lost one in three visits. Home visits are risky for completion.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Toshio,,The car park fills before eleven. Any new outpatient service will face immediate capacity issues.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,Data agreements take fourteen months. Any program relying on outside surgeries is too slow.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Yumi,,Therapy staffing is critical. A day rehab unit would strain the remaining physiotherapists.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Servas,,On-site sessions bill at standard rates. We need a program that fits in existing rooms.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"Chronic care coordination could consolidate appointments, reducing the need for new rooms.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Toshio,,But coordinators need space. The booking system must be able to track their work.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"If we assign coordinators internally, we avoid the data agreement delays with outside bodies.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Yumi,,It also avoids the therapy staffing crisis. We can use the midwifery slack for perinatal support.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Servas,,Chronic care coordination seems to fit the financial and staffing constraints best.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
