64,3,1,talk,Servas,,It generates on-site revenue and fits the reduced development budget.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Asuka,,I agree with Servas. The financial model is the strongest for D.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"I am concerned about the booking system, but D is the most manageable.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,D is the only option that doesn't rely on external parties for core operations.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Yumi,,I support D. It protects the therapy team and uses existing staff effectively.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Servas,,I vote for D. It is the most sustainable and financially viable option.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Asuka,,I will vote for D. It has the best evidence base from the readmission trial.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
